IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-10.l4 -- ARTICLE 10: PERSONAL DATA RELATING TO CRIMINAL CONVICTIONS AND OFFENCES.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- Whose duty: the text names no party for either sentence ("shall be carried out only ...", "shall be kept
-- only ..."); the controller is the natural bearer but is not named, so only decision functions are written
-- (no regulative rule).  Who may rely on it: the data subject.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 10, first sentence: processing based on Article 6(1)`

-- src:137 | Processing of personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures based on Article 6(1) shall be carried out only under the control of official authority or when the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law providing for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects. Any comprehensive register of criminal convictions shall be kept only under the control of official authority.
@ref Art 10, first sentence (src:137)
GIVEN `the personal data relate to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on Article 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is carried out under the control of official authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that law provides for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10 the processing of personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures meets the condition of Art 10` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data relate to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures` AND `the processing is based on Article 6(1)`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Processing of personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures based on Article 6(1)"; other processing is not spoken of here
        IF `the processing is carried out under the control of official authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law` AND `that law provides for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only"): "shall be carried out only under the control of official authority or when the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law providing for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects"

§ `Article 10, second sentence: the comprehensive register`

-- src:137 | Processing of personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences or related security measures based on Article 6(1) shall be carried out only under the control of official authority or when the processing is authorised by Union or Member State law providing for appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of data subjects. Any comprehensive register of criminal convictions shall be kept only under the control of official authority.
@ref Art 10, second sentence (src:137)
GIVEN `the register is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the register is kept under the control of official authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 10 the comprehensive register of criminal convictions is kept only under the control of official authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the register is a comprehensive register of criminal convictions`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any comprehensive register of criminal convictions"; another register is not spoken of
        IF `the register is kept under the control of official authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "only"): "Any comprehensive register of criminal convictions shall be kept only under the control of official authority."
